}}|subdivision_type1=[[Communities of Balisca|Community]]|subdivision_name1={{flag|Cerdanya}}|area_km2=38,097.11|population_census=1,265,282|population_census_year=2020|regional_languages=|common_languages={{W|Aranese dialect|Aranese}}, [[Baliscano]], {{W|Catalan language|Catalan}} and {{W|Mapuche language|Mapudungun}}|cctld=.mal|mapsize=280px}}'''Máfil''' ({{Literal translation|embraced between waters}}) is a [[Regions of Balisca|region]] of [[Cerdanya]], within the [[Balisca|Baliscan Confederation]]. It borders [[Provence]] and [[Muntanya]] to the north/northeast and [[Pigüe]] to the south.

Máfil's economy, because of its important geographic location, is mainly based on a well-developed service sector, especially commerce, tourism, and trading. The construction of the [[Pirihueico Canal]] and military installations after the [[South Atlantic War]] has given rise to large construction projects. 

